<div class="bb-grid"><form id="carrier-feed-form" class="panel extension-form"><h2>Measurement connection</h2><label class="check"><input name="enabled" type="checkbox"> Use fresh measured frequency when available</label><label>Station JSON feed URL<input name="url" type="url" placeholder="https://your-station.example/readings.json"></label><label>Maximum age, seconds<input name="max_age" type="number" min="30" max="3600" value="300"></label><button class="button primary" type="submit">Save connection</button><button type="button" class="button" id="carrier-feed-refresh">Fetch reading now</button><p>Checks every minute. Stale, absent or invalid readings fall back to the fixed 7.83 Hz oscillator. The default connection reads the documented Tomsk spectrogram extraction series from Ressonância Schumann Hoje. It is a derived station peak, not raw sensor samples; its actual age is shown.</p><details><summary>Sensor feed format</summary><pre>{"kind":"measured","station":"Station name","frequency_hz":7.8,"measured_at":"ISO timestamp with timezone"}</pre><p>The timestamp and frequency must come from an actual measurement. Custom feeds must provide numeric measurements. The built-in feed is labelled spectrogram-derived.</p></details></form><article class="panel extension-form"><h2>Current carrier</h2><p id="carrier-reading-status" role="status"></p><pre id="carrier-reading-receipt" class="bb-output"></pre><p>This controls the app’s software pulse timing. A remote station measurement does not make this computer an electromagnetic sensor or transmitter.</p></article></div>`,
