put name="compare" type="checkbox" checked> Compare both uncertainty settings</label><p>Known harmful candidates are excluded in both modes. Forced trials retain unresolved warnings and never send their output automatically. Unexamined groups stay visible and can be continued.</p><div class="button-row"><button class="button primary" type="submit">Assess & forecast</button><button class="button" type="button" id="predictive-stop">Pause</button></div><p id="predictive-status" role="status"></p></form>
<article class="panel extension-form"><h2>Assessment & comparison</h2><label>Run<select id="predictive-job"></select></label><div class="button-row"><button class="button" id="predictive-resume" disabled>Continue paused run</button><button class="button" id="predictive-download" disabled>Download full evidence</button><button class="button primary" id="predictive-cast" disabled>Send resolved result to chirals</button></div><pre id="predictive-summary" class="bb-output" tabindex="0"></pre><p>The whole neural field contributes alongside case-specific model votes. Evidence gaps and disagreement remain uncertain. Resolved groups share a forecast; their single-bit decisions are marked as inherited, not independently predicted.</p></article></div>
